# Forge 2.0 Master Directive

Repo: `ForgePS/IndustrialSafety2.0`. Branch: `forge-creator-2.0`. Full text: `docs/FORGE_NEXT_LEVEL_FUNCTIONALITY_MASTER_DIRECTIVE.md`.

## Definition of done

A feature is complete only when this path works:

`UI → server action/API → authz → validation → DB → related modules → activity/audit → notifications/automation → reporting/AI context → automated tests`

Not complete because a page renders.

## Absolute: no shells

Do not create placeholders, fake KPIs/alerts/rows, localStorage-as-SOR, static arrays as backend data, mock production APIs, TODO workflow buttons, non-persisting forms, Coming Soon, or duplicate personnel/location/task/permission systems.

`custom_data jsonb` is only for tenant-configurable custom fields. Core operational data uses explicit relational structures.

## Architecture & security

Reuse existing Forge systems (`getTenantContext`, `requireTenantPermission`, `getEffectiveTenantAccess`, Creator, Personnel, Training, Incidents, Inspections, Assets, QR, LOTO, Tasks, Support, AI). Never parallel implementations.

Every operational table needs authoritative `organization_id`, RLS, and server-side validation of org/location/division/personnel/asset IDs. Never trust browser-supplied tenant IDs. Service-role never replaces permission checks.

Order: auth → active org → feature → permission → scope → relationship validation → sensitive-data rules → business rule → mutation. Cross-tenant UUID access must fail.

## Lifecycle, audit, attachments

No physical delete of regulated records in normal ops (archive/retire/void/cancel). Status transitions: validated, permissioned, scoped, business-ruled, timestamped, actor-identified, activity + audit.

Reuse private attachment/authorization patterns. Prefer structured evidence relationships over URL-in-text.

## AI / Guardian / exclusions

AI uses existing capability registry, approved-action queue, and domain actions — never unrestricted DB mutation. Guardian is a cross-module signal engine, not a chatbot. Do not build CV camera monitoring or wearable/connected-worker monitoring.

## Sprint gates (required)

Before declaring complete: clean DB migrate+seed, type-check, production build, Playwright smoke, authz/cross-tenant tests. Report the 16-point completion checklist. If incomplete: `SPRINT NOT COMPLETE`.
